epression (1.43; 95% CI: 1.41–1.45). Table 2. Adjusted odds ratios for factors influencing use of any imaging (sample before matching). Any Imaging Chest Imaging Neuroimaging Imaging ED Imaging Variable OR 95% CI OR 95% CI OR 95% CI OR 95% CI Anxiety 1.24 1.22–1.26 1.06 1.03–1.09 1.48 1.45–1.51 1.46 1.43–1.48 Depression 1.43 1.41–1.45 1.08 1.06–1.11 1.83 1.80–1.86 1.55 1.53–1.57 Age 1.00 1.00–1.00 1.00 1.00–1.00 1.01 1.01–1.01 1.00 1.00–1.00 Rural (as opposed to Urban) 0.99 0.98–1.00 0.96 0.94–0.97 0.96 0.95–0.97 1.07 1.06–1.08 Commercial (as opposed to Medicare) 1.07 1.06–1.09 0.77 0.75–0.80 0.81 0.79–0.83 0.76 0.75–0.77 Plan Type: HMO (as opposed to FFS) 0.72 0.70–0.73 0.87 0.84–0.90 0.83 0.81–0.85 0.86 0.85–0.88 Plan Type: PPO (as opposed to FFS) 1.09 1.07–1.11 1.13 1.09–1.16 0.96 0.94–0.98 0.97 0.96–0.99 Female 1.40 1.39–1.41 0.91 0.90–0.92 1.15 1.14–1.16 1.14 1.13–1.15 Below $40k Income 0.96 0.95–0.97 1.00 0.98–1.01 1.02 1.01–1.03 1.09 1.08–1.10 2017 Cardiology Claims 3.31 3.29–3.34 3.11 3.04–3.18 2.26 2.22–2.29 2.27 2.25–2.30 2017 Imaging Claims 3.24 3.22–3.26 1.66 1.63–1.68 2.11 2.09–2.13 2.17 2.15–2.18 2017 Oncology Claims 1.86 1.81–1.91 0.99 0.96–1.02 1.45 1.41–1.48 1.25 1.22–1.27 2017 CAD 1.21 1.20–1.22 2.54 2.51–2.57 1.27 1.26–1.28 1.35 1.34–1.36 2017 CHF 1.16 1.14–1.17 1.14 1.12–1.16 1.37 1.35–1.39 1.62 1.60–1.63 2017 COPD 1.32 1.31–1.34 1.13 1.12–1.15 1.23 1.22–1.25 1.56 1.54–1.57 2017 Diabetes 1.02 1.02–1.03 1.25 1.23–1.26 1.20 1.19–1.21 1.24 1.23–1.25 Prevalence of Obesity (scaled) 3.85 3.76–3.95 1.62 1.55–1.69 1.66 1.61–1.72 1.81 1.76–1.86 Region: 1 (as opposed to 4) 1.85 1.75–1.95 0.93 0.83–1.04 1.40 1.30–1.50 1.64 1.55–1.73 Region: 2 (as opposed to 4) 2.19 2.10–2.29 1.44 1.35–1.55 1.39 1.31–1.47 1.43 1.36–1.49 Region: 3 (as opposed to 4) 1.32 1.30–1.33 0.99 0.97–1.01 1.14 1.12–1.16 1.33 1.32–1.35 Region: 5 (as opposed to 4) 1.03 1.03–1.04 0.87 0.85–0.88 1.05 1.03–1.06 1.22 1.20–1.23 Region: 6 (as opposed to 4) 1.12 1.11–1.13 1.13 1.11–1.14 1.02 1.0