as stirred at 37°C overnight, and reaction completion was confirmed by UPLC. The crude reaction was purified directly by preparative HPLC and lyophilized to yield title compound as a white solid (2.1 mg, 15%). 1 H NMR (600 MHz, DMSO) δ 10.97 (s, 1H), 7.59 (d, J = 8.3 Hz, 1H), 7.32 (s, 1H), 7.21 (dd, J = 7.5, 1.7 Hz, 2H), 7.16 (td, J = 7.8, 1.8 Hz, 1H), 6.87 (d, J = 1.1 Hz, 1H), 6.81 (td, J = 7.5, 1.1 Hz, 1H), 5.08 (dd, J = 13.3, 5.2 Hz, 1H), 4.30 (dd, 2H), 4.02 (d, J = 4.7 Hz, 2H), 3.84 (t, J = 6.4 Hz, 2H), 2.95 – 2.86 (m, 1H), 2.62 – 2.55 (m, 1H), 2.43 – 2.34 (m, 1H), 2.02 – 1.92 (m, 1H), 1.68 – 1.59 (m, 2H), 0.91 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H). 13 C NMR (151 MHz, DMSO) δ 172.9, 171.1, 168.0, 165.5, 155.8, 143.4, 128.3, 128.2, 125.3, 123.7, 119.8, 117.5, 111.5, 111.2, 68.9, 5.5, 47.0, 40.6, 40.1, 31.2, 22.5, 22.0, 10.4. HRMS analysis: expected 487.1646, found 487.1647 [M+H] + Supplementary Material Supplementary Figure 1 Supplementary Figure 1. Cells are deficient in CRBN. Immunoblot analysis for cereblon expression in knockout cell lines. NIHMS1994268-supplement-Supplementary_Figure_1.pdf (555.4KB, pdf) Supplementary Figure 2 Supplementary Figure 2. Both N- and C-terminal GSPT1-HiBiT fusions are degraded by CC-885. Results of 10-point dose response of CC-885 treatment in HiBiT expressing cell lines, as approximated by HiBiT assay (means ± SEM, n = 3) NIHMS1994268-supplement-Supplementary_Figure_2.pdf (560KB, pdf) Supplementary Figure 3 Supplementary Figure 3. IKZF1-HiBiT degradation in MV4;11 cells. (A) Results of 10-point dose response of CC-885 treatment in HiBiT expressing cell lines, as approximated by HiBiT assay (means ± SEM, n = 3) (B) Immunoblot analysis of IKZF1 in MV4;11 cell lysates treated with vehicle, compound, or lenalidomide (3 μM, 3 hr). NIHMS1994268-supplement-Supplementary_Figure_3.pdf (596.6KB, pdf) Acknowledgement This work was supported by the Ono Pharmaceutical Foundation and The Baxter Foundation Young Investigator Award (M.A.E.), as well as K99GM1387